WEBVTT

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:08.900
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Bank holiday or not, here we are. Can you all hear me?</v>

00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:16.469
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, unfortunately. Had all these weekend plans, barbecue, bit of gardening. Weather had other ideas.</v>

00:00:17.359 --> 00:00:19.809
<v Fiona Doyle>You didn't actually get the barbecue out?</v>

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:27.359
<v Callum Reid>Got as far as taking the cover off. Put it straight back on. Very productive weekend.</v>

00:00:27.969 --> 00:00:33.920
<v Sarah Okafor>Lovely. Meanwhile the heating in the portakabin thinks it's December. I'm sitting here with the door open.</v>

00:00:35.049 --> 00:00:39.250
<v Marcus Hale>So that's where all the heat's going. Certainly isn't reaching my end.</v>

00:00:40.329 --> 00:00:44.530
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Morning—sorry, Teams picked the wrong microphone again. Am I coming through now?</v>

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:48.719
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep, you're fine now. Bit echoey, but fine.</v>

00:00:49.409 --> 00:00:54.310
<v Tomasz Nowak>Better than mine. I've got about three people coming out of one little speaker.</v>

00:00:54.689 --> 00:01:00.990
<v Sarah Okafor>Right. Aisha Begum and Jamie Brennan aren't with us today. We've got everyone else, so let's crack on.</v>

00:01:02.649 --> 00:01:05.450
<v Fiona Doyle>Yep, I'm here. Calendar's open, coffee's mostly working.</v>

00:01:07.250 --> 00:01:15.299
<v Sarah Okafor>First, I'm not sending that shift handover report round after all. The other shift already sorted it, so there's no point duplicating it.</v>

00:01:16.689 --> 00:01:18.439
<v Marcus Hale>Fair enough. One copy's plenty.</v>

00:01:19.269 --> 00:01:26.620
<v Marcus Hale>And, um, the new starters' training records—I've got the first half done. There's a fair bit left in the second half.</v>

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:30.799
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah, those folders are thicker than they look.</v>

00:01:32.049 --> 00:01:40.799
<v Callum Reid>My contractor booking for the Arburg is stuck. Waiting on the permit to be signed; I can't get any further with it until that's through.</v>

00:01:42.890 --> 00:01:44.640
<v Sarah Okafor>Understood. That's the hold-up, then.</v>

00:01:45.269 --> 00:01:49.469
<v Olumide Adeyemi>The near-miss write-up for the Arburg is finished, though. All signed off.</v>

00:01:50.180 --> 00:01:51.379
<v Tomasz Nowak>Ah, good. Cheers.</v>

00:01:51.930 --> 00:01:58.930
<v Olumide Adeyemi>And that monthly fire alarm test we had sitting without an owner—I'll take it on. Put Mide against that one.</v>

00:01:59.469 --> 00:02:00.670
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, that's agreed.</v>

00:02:02.920 --> 00:02:13.770
<v Sarah Okafor>Doyler asked me to pass on that the risk assessment update for work on the Injection Moulding Line 2 needs to move off her list. Reidy, can you take that over?</v>

00:02:15.930 --> 00:02:18.729
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, I'll take over the risk assessment update.</v>

00:02:20.379 --> 00:02:21.580
<v Fiona Doyle>Cheers, appreciate that.</v>

00:02:22.770 --> 00:02:28.370
<v Fiona Doyle>Oh, and I tested the turbine one gas valve yesterday. It's all fine now, that's sorted.</v>

00:02:30.210 --> 00:02:33.009
<v Marcus Hale>Good news. Nice to hear something behaved itself.</v>

00:02:35.469 --> 00:02:38.620
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, onto the new bits. What have we got?</v>

00:02:39.169 --> 00:02:43.719
<v Tomasz Nowak>I'll check the guarding on the stacker next week. Normal priority, that one.</v>

00:02:46.150 --> 00:02:50.699
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Tomasz Nowak. Guarding check on the stacker, next week, normal priority. Agreed.</v>

00:02:52.439 --> 00:02:55.240
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yep. Nothing more urgent than that being suggested.</v>

00:02:55.789 --> 00:02:56.990
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, that's sensible.</v>

00:02:57.439 --> 00:03:03.039
<v Sarah Okafor>Tomasz Nowak, can you organise the toolbox talk for the team first thing tomorrow as well?</v>

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:09.300
<v Tomasz Nowak>Sorry, no, I can't take organising that on. I haven't got the capacity for it.</v>

00:03:11.789 --> 00:03:17.389
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay. Doyler, can you take that instead—organise the toolbox talk for the team, first thing tomorrow?</v>

00:03:19.740 --> 00:03:22.539
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah, I'll organise it. First thing tomorrow, understood.</v>

00:03:24.379 --> 00:03:26.129
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks. That's with you, then.</v>

00:03:28.090 --> 00:03:32.289
<v Fiona Doyle>Always nice getting the one where everyone looks thrilled to be there.</v>

00:03:33.509 --> 00:03:36.659
<v Callum Reid>That's just my face before breakfast, to be fair.</v>

00:03:39.090 --> 00:03:47.139
<v Sarah Okafor>Tom, can you swap the filter on the Line 1 Hydraulic Power Unit by end of day? That one's safety critical, straight away.</v>

00:03:48.430 --> 00:03:54.030
<v Tomasz Nowak>Right, so that's an immediate start, not something to leave until the end of the shift?</v>

00:03:56.069 --> 00:03:59.919
<v Sarah Okafor>Exactly. Straight away, with the filter swapped by end of day.</v>

00:04:01.659 --> 00:04:08.310
<v Tomasz Nowak>Understood. I'll swap the filter on the Line 1 Hydraulic Power Unit. Straight away, done by end of day.</v>

00:04:09.009 --> 00:04:12.509
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah, safety critical takes it out of the ordinary queue.</v>

00:04:13.539 --> 00:04:15.289
<v Tomasz Nowak>Absolutely. No argument from me.</v>

00:04:17.459 --> 00:04:27.610
<v Sarah Okafor>And Tommo, can you go to the treatment plant to pick up the replacement parts for the main water valve by the 28th? That one's safety critical, straight away.</v>

00:04:29.110 --> 00:04:34.360
<v Tomasz Nowak>Just checking—you're asking me to collect the parts, not fit them as part of this?</v>

00:04:34.980 --> 00:04:41.980
<v Sarah Okafor>Correct, collection of the replacement parts. Treat it as safety critical straight away; the collection deadline is by the 28th.</v>

00:04:42.529 --> 00:04:51.629
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yep, I'll go to the treatment plant and pick up the replacement parts for the main water valve by the 28th. Safety critical, straight away—got it.</v>

00:04:53.959 --> 00:04:59.560
<v Fiona Doyle>Three versions of your name this morning. Teams will think we've got a bigger maintenance department.</v>

00:05:01.680 --> 00:05:04.129
<v Tomasz Nowak>Same bloke, sadly. Same pair of hands.</v>

00:05:06.079 --> 00:05:08.529
<v Sarah Okafor>Quite. Everyone clear on what's been agreed?</v>

00:05:09.819 --> 00:05:11.220
<v Marcus Hale>Yep, clear from me.</v>

00:05:13.629 --> 00:05:15.029
<v Olumide Adeyemi>All clear here too.</v>

00:05:16.550 --> 00:05:20.399
<v Callum Reid>Yeah. And the sun's come out now we're all indoors. Typical.</v>

00:05:22.720 --> 00:05:25.870
<v Sarah Okafor>Of course it has. Right, thanks everyone. That's us.</v>

00:05:27.639 --> 00:05:28.839
<v Fiona Doyle>Cheers, all.</v>
